@*
    The one way that the app reaches the storage of a browser.

    A browser can refuse its storage, and each caller then keeps the choice for
    this page alone. That rule lives here, so no caller states it twice.

    It stands first in the head, because the theme script reads a key before
    the first paint.
*@

<script>
    window.tracerStorage = {
        read: function (key) {
            try {
                return window.localStorage.getItem(key);
            } catch (unreachableStorage) {
                return null;
            }
        },
        write: function (key, value) {
            try {
                window.localStorage.setItem(key, value);
            } catch (unreachableStorage) {
                /* The choice holds for this page alone. */
            }
        }
    };
</script>
